 "note": "iropmap.py -- read the cgc-IR-operation -> GLASM-opcode table out of the image.\n\nf_7100f10a30 is the step that turns ONE cgc IR node into GLASM instructions\n(notes/33, notes/34).  It takes the node's operation from `node[16] >> 16`,\nrange-checks it against 0xca and dispatches through a halfword jump table in\n.rodata at 0x11bdf94 anchored at 0xf10b1c.  The simple arms are three\ninstructions -- `mov w8, <GLASM opcode>` / `sub w9, w3, <family base>` / `b` --\nand the pair (w8, w9) becomes the descriptor f_7100f13410 hands to the node\nbuilder, whose W1 lands in node[8].  So those arms ARE the map, read rather\nthan fitted.  Arms that do more than that are reported by address, not guessed.\n",
